From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Swostik Acharya <swosacha@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:57:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] feat(qti): add secure HSR SMMU support

Program the secure SMMU implementation-defined registers on nord in
BL31: the always-on APPS TCU and PCIe registers via qti_smmu_init(),
and the GPU SMMU registers via qti_smmu_clocked_init() from
clocked_boot_init(), where the clock back-end holds GPU CX powered with
register retention so the writes land.

Add the nord register tables (drivers/qti/smmu/nord/smmu_cfg.c and its
header), build the SMMU driver for nord via smmu.mk, and wire the GPU
clocked init into the common BL31 setup.

Depends on the nord platform and clock support (change 55212) and the
nord RPMh target support.

Change-Id: Icfb093e9b5e952832f9c48d8dbf3e862e9319506
Signed-off-by: Swostik Acharya <swosacha@qti.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/56585
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/pull/133]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
